Quick update on the TeamCity inherited parameter issue.

I was able to identify the root cause. The build number format was still referencing the legacy %Environment% parameter, which prevented TeamCity from deleting it.

After updating the build number format to reference %environmentName%, I was able to successfully remove the old parameter from the detached AdminCopy configuration.

I’ve also verified that the old Environment dropdown is no longer appearing in the custom build parameters. I’ll apply the same changes to the original Admin configuration and validate the Run/Customize dialogs and nightly triggers.

Thanks, Ryan, for the suggestion to test with a detached configuration!